{
  "id": 461866854,
  "iid": 23799,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "RDM: Updates for E1.20 2025 and E1.37-5",
  "description": "Add new packet types and enum values from E1.20 2025 and E1.37-5.\\\nSpec links: https://tsp.esta.org/tsp/documents/published_docs.php\n\nShould close https://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/issues/20085, (possibly) https://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/issues/19254, and is a partial fix for https://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/issues/20611.\n\nAlso adds a field to mark dynamic UIDs, and fixes the checksum offset when the packet's parameter data length doesn't match what it should for the packet type.\\\nI have rearranged some of the E1.37 and E1.33 packet types to better match the spec order to make it easier to read.\n\n## Sample Capture:\n\n[rdm_pids5_small.pcapng.gz](/uploads/449495a67a6e99561c50d38c7b847925/rdm_pids5_small.pcapng.gz) - Does some of E1.37-5. I was unable to find any for E1.20 as it's so new.\\\nI have also tested with various other RDM packets from old issues/MRs and they all look good.\n\n## ACK_OVERFLOW Handling\n\nThis implements the naive handling scheme described here: https://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/issues/20611#note_2648737457, with some heuristics to try and detect when a response is the first packet.\n\nThere are still situations where full assembly would be helpful, and some of the new packet types (PACKED_PID\\_\\*) cannot be properly dissected without the information from the earlier packet.",
  "state": "merged",
