    {
      "id": "bcfc650cf3f3d923fa73ea08be86bd642fa75428",
      "individual_note": false,
      "resolvable": true,
      "resolved": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 3146817972,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Coverity noticed an implicit fallthrough:\n\n```c\n_____________________________________________________________________________________________\n*** CID 1684197:         Control flow issues  (MISSING_BREAK)\n/builds/wireshark/wireshark/epan/dissectors/packet-rdm.c: 2997             in dissect_rdm_pd_queued_message_sensor_subscribe()\n2991     }\n2992     \n2993     static unsigned\n2994     dissect_rdm_pd_queued_message_sensor_subscribe(tvbuff_t *tvb, unsigned offset, proto_tree *tree, uint8_t cc, uint8_t len)\n2995     {\n2996       switch(cc) {\n>>>     CID 1684197:         Control flow issues  (MISSING_BREAK)\n>>>     The case for value \"48\" is not terminated by a \"break\" statement.\n2997       case RDM_CC_SET_COMMAND:\n2998         proto_tree_add_item(tree, hf_rdm_pd_sensor_subscribe_action, tvb, offset, 1, ENC_BIG_ENDIAN);\n2999         offset += 1;\n3000       case RDM_CC_GET_COMMAND_RESPONSE:\n3001         while (len >= 1) {\n3002           proto_tree_add_item(tree, hf_rdm_pd_sensor_nr, tvb, offset, 1, ENC_BIG_ENDIAN);\n```\n\nIs fallthrough intentional, or not? I'm not sure why gcc didn't warn about this, as we enable -Wextra. We don't enable -Wimplicit-fallthrough in general because, e.g., clang doesn't recognize comments that indicate fallthrough unlike gcc, though we could define something in `ws_attributes` to use `__attribute__ ((fallthrough));` for gcc/Clang. MSVC doesn't enable it by default.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
          "created_at": "2026-03-10T15:31:33.524Z",
          "updated_at": "2026-03-10T18:50:28.557Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 461866854,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": false,
          "resolved_by": null,
          "resolved_at": null,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 23799,
          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 3147768591,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Fallthrough is intentional.\n\nSet has an 'action' an both have a list of 'sensor_numbers'.\n\nLooks like line 2999 is missing a `len -= 1` as well.",
          "author": {
            "id": 31448333,
            "username": "mattmdev",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Matt Morris",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/9fab9b68b89a123a69e4d819fae337fb1fb365826281d802ee06504af8a753b7?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/mattmdev"
          },
          "created_at": "2026-03-10T18:50:28.503Z",
          "updated_at": "2026-03-10T18:50:28.503Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 461866854,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": false,
          "resolved_by": null,
          "resolved_at": null,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 23799,
          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 3147922788,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "OK, if you a MR to add the `len -= 1`, please add a comment like `/* FALLTHROUGH */` or similar.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
